-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 5: ss 54 to 64, the truck system,
-- which governs how a workman's salary is paid and spent.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file (script-generated); every quotation in
-- a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment is a phrase of it (checked by a script).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its
-- own words.  NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts and is never to
-- be read as no.  "marginal (a)" or "marginal (b)" marks the branches that rest on
-- one of the two readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).
--
-- WORKMEN ONLY.  Part 5 speaks of "a workman" (s 2(1) "workman", the keel).  Each function
-- takes "the person is a workman" as a plain fact, so the caller applies the keel's test first.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 5 Truck system, ss 54 to 64`

§§ `s 54 Agreements to pay salary otherwise than in legal tender illegal`

-- src:2373 | 54. The salary of a workman must be payable in legal tender and not
-- src:2374 | otherwise and if in any contract of service the whole or any part of the
-- src:2375 | salary is made payable in any other manner the contract of service is
-- src:2376 | illegal and void.
@ref s 54 (src:2373-2376)
GIVEN `the person is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 the salary may be made payable otherwise than in legal tender` MEANS
    IF `the person is a workman`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The salary of a workman must be payable in legal tender and not otherwise" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 54 speaks only of "a workman"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 54 (src:2373-2376)
GIVEN `the person is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the whole or any part of the salary is made payable in the contract of service in a manner other than legal tender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 the contract of service is illegal and void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 54 speaks only of "a workman" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF NOT `the person is a workman` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the whole or any part of the salary is made payable in the contract of service in a manner other than legal tender` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if in any contract of service the whole or any part of the salary is made payable in any other manner the contract of service is illegal and void" -- an unmet "if"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 55 Agreements as to place and manner, etc., of spending salary illegal`

-- src:2381 | 55. A contract of service must not contain any terms as to the place
-- src:2382 | at which, or the manner in which, or the person with whom, any
-- src:2383 | salary paid to the workman is to be expended and every contract of
-- src:2384 | service containing such terms is illegal and void.
@ref s 55 (src:2381-2384)
GIVEN `the contract of service is with a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service contains a term as to the place at which, the manner in which, or the person with whom, any salary paid to the workman is to be expended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 the contract of service may contain the term` MEANS
    IF `the contract of service is with a workman` AND `the contract of service contains a term as to the place at which, the manner in which, or the person with whom, any salary paid to the workman is to be expended`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A contract of service must not contain any terms as to the place at which, or the manner in which, or the person with whom, any salary paid to the workman is to be expended" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 55 speaks only of terms as to the place, manner or person with whom the salary of a workman is to be expended
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 55 (src:2381-2384)
GIVEN `the contract of service is with a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service contains a term as to the place at which, the manner in which, or the person with whom, any salary paid to the workman is to be expended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 the contract of service is illegal and void` MEANS
    IF `the contract of service is with a workman` AND `the contract of service contains a term as to the place at which, the manner in which, or the person with whom, any salary paid to the workman is to be expended`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every contract of service containing such terms is illegal and void"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 56 Salary to be paid entirely in legal tender`

-- src:2388 | 56. Except where otherwise expressly permitted by the provisions
-- src:2389 | of this Act, the entire amount of the salary earned by, or payable to,
-- src:2390 | any workman in respect of any work done by him or her must be
-- src:2391 | actually paid to him or her in legal tender, and every payment of, or on
-- src:2392 | account of, any such salary made in any other form is illegal and void.
@ref s 56 (src:2388-2392)
GIVEN `the amount of the salary earned by or payable to the workman in respect of work done` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount actually paid to the workman in legal tender` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 56 the entire amount of the salary has been actually paid in legal tender` MEANS
    `the amount actually paid to the workman in legal tender` AT LEAST `the amount of the salary earned by or payable to the workman in respect of work done`

@ref s 56 (src:2388-2392)
GIVEN `the person is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made in a form other than legal tender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act expressly permits the payment in that form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56 the payment is illegal and void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 56 speaks only of "any workman" and of "every payment of, or on account of, any such salary made in any other form" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF (NOT `the person is a workman`) OR (NOT `the payment is made in a form other than legal tender`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where otherwise expressly permitted by the provisions of this Act" -- an "except where" read like "unless": the rule is lifted
        IF `this Act expressly permits the payment in that form` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 57 Recovery of salary not paid in legal tender`

-- src:2396 | 57. Every workman is entitled to recover in any court or before the
-- src:2397 | Commissioner, acting under section 115, so much of his or her salary
-- src:2398 | exclusive of sums lawfully deducted in accordance with the
-- src:2399 | provisions of this Act as has not been actually paid to him or her
-- src:2400 | in legal tender.
@ref s 57 (src:2396-2400)
GIVEN `the person is a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the salary earned` IS A NUMBER
      `the sums lawfully deducted in accordance with the provisions of this Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount actually paid in legal tender` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57 the amount of salary the workman is entitled to recover` MEANS
    IF `the person is a workman`
    THEN JUST (max 0 ((`the salary earned` MINUS `the sums lawfully deducted in accordance with the provisions of this Act`) MINUS `the amount actually paid in legal tender`))
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every workman is entitled to recover"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 58 Interest on advances forbidden`

DECLARE `s 58 Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 58 the employer`

DECLARE `s 58 Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 58 make a deduction by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of an advance of salary made to a workman`

-- src:2407 | 58. An employer must not make any deduction by way of discount,
-- src:2408 | interest or any similar charge on account of any advance of salary
-- src:2409 | made to any workman.
@ref s 58 (src:2407-2409)
GIVEN `the deduction is by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of an advance of salary made to a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 58 the employer may make the deduction` MEANS
    IF `the deduction is by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of an advance of salary made to a workman`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An employer must not make any deduction by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of any advance of salary made to any workman" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 58 speaks only of a deduction by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on an advance of salary to a workman
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The prohibition of section 58, derived from the flat negative (ruling N2): the employer is the
-- bearer, and making the deduction is the breach.
@ref s 58 (src:2407-2409)
GIVEN `the deduction is by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of an advance of salary made to a workman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 58 Actor` `s 58 Action`
`s 58 the employer's prohibition on a deduction by way of interest on an advance` MEANS
    IF `the deduction is by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of an advance of salary made to a workman`
    THEN PARTY `s 58 the employer`
         SHANT `s 58 make a deduction by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of an advance of salary made to a workman`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 58 the employer` BECAUSE "the employer made a deduction by way of discount, interest or any similar charge on account of an advance of salary made to a workman"
    ELSE FULFILLED

