`s 60(1) this Part prevents the employer from establishing or permitting the shop or canteen` MEANS
    IF `the employer establishes or permits to be established a shop or a canteen for the sale of foodstuffs, provisions, meals or refreshments`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Part prevents the employer from establishing or permitting to be established a shop or a canteen for the sale of foodstuffs, provisions, meals or refreshments" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks only of a shop or a canteen for the sale of foodstuffs, provisions, meals or refreshments
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 60(1) (src:2422-2427)
