    IF `the workman is compelled by a contract of service to purchase goods at the shop or canteen`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a workman must not be compelled by any contract of service to purchase any goods at that shop or canteen" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) forbids compulsion by a contract of service
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 60(1) (src:2422-2427)
GIVEN `the thing sold at the shop or canteen is noxious drugs or intoxicating liquor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1) noxious drugs and intoxicating liquor may be sold at the shop or canteen` MEANS
    IF `the thing sold at the shop or canteen is noxious drugs or intoxicating liquor`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "noxious drugs and intoxicating liquor must not be sold at any such shop or canteen" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) forbids only the sale of noxious drugs and intoxicating liquor
    ELSE NOTHING

