    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s 61 Offence`

-- src:2437 | 61. Any employer who enters into any contract of service or gives
-- src:2438 | any remuneration for service contrary to the provisions of this Part or
-- src:2439 | declared by this Part to be illegal or receives any payment from any
-- src:2440 | workman contrary to the provisions of this Part or contravenes
-- src:2441 | section 60(2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:2442 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000, and for a second or
-- src:2443 | subsequent offence to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:2444 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 61 (src:2437-2444)
GIVEN `the employer enters into a contract of service or gives remuneration for service contrary to the provisions of Part 5 or declared by Part 5 to be illegal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer receives a payment from a workman contrary to the provisions of Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer contravenes section 60(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61 the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer enters into a contract of service or gives remuneration for service contrary to the provisions of Part 5 or declared by Part 5 to be illegal` OR `the employer receives a payment from a workman contrary to the provisions of Part 5` OR `the employer contravenes section 60(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any employer who enters into any contract of service or gives any remuneration for service contrary to the provisions of this Part or declared by this Part to be illegal or receives any payment from any workman contrary to the provisions of this Part or contravenes section 60(2)"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 61 (src:2437-2444)
GIVEN `the employer is guilty of an offence under section 61` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`
`s 61 the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction"
        IF NOT `the employer is guilty of an offence under section 61` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the offence is a second or subsequent offence` THEN JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 10000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12)
        OTHERWISE JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING)

§§ `s 63 Payment of salary through bank`

-- src:2453 | 63.—(1) Nothing in section 54 or 56 operates so as to render
-- src:2454 | unlawful or invalid any payment of salary by the employer to the
-- src:2455 | workman in any of the following ways:
-- src:2457 | (a) payment into an account at a bank in Singapore, being an
-- src:2458 | account in the name of the workman or an account in the
-- src:2459 | name of the workman jointly with one or more other
-- src:2460 | persons;
-- src:2462 | (b) payment by cheque made payable to or to the order of the
-- src:2463 | workman.
@ref s 63(1) (src:2453-2463)
GIVEN `the salary is paid into an account at a bank in Singapore, being an account in the name of the workman or jointly with one or more other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the salary is paid by cheque made payable to or to the order of the workman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(1) section 54 or 56 renders the payment of salary unlawful or invalid` MEANS
    IF `the salary is paid into an account at a bank in Singapore, being an account in the name of the workman or jointly with one or more other persons` OR `the salary is paid by cheque made payable to or to the order of the workman`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 54 or 56 operates so as to render unlawful or invalid any payment of salary by the employer to the workman in any of the following ways" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) names two ways of payment, a bank account in the workman's name and a cheque payable to the workman
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The amount recoverable under s 57 is cut by what was paid in the ways of subsection (1).
-- src:2465 | (2) Where the salary or part thereof has been paid in any of the ways
-- src:2466 | set out in subsection (1), section 57 does not operate to give a right of
-- src:2467 | recovery of so much of the salary as has been so paid.
@ref s 63(2) (src:2465-2467)
GIVEN `the answer of s 57 the amount of salary the workman is entitled to recover` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the part of the salary paid in a way set out in subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 63(2) the amount of salary the workman has a right of recovery of under section 57` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 57 the amount of salary the workman is entitled to recover`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside this subsection): the amount under section 57 is that section's answer, which may be none
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (max 0 (amount MINUS `the part of the salary paid in a way set out in subsection (1)`))

